{"answer": "**Participants in the \u201cBudget numbers\u201d thread & their commitments**\n\n| Person | Project/Line they\u2019ll handle (commitment) | Source |\n|--------|------------------------------------------|--------|\n| **Alice Ander** | \u2022 Put proposals into the thread by Thursday.<br>\u2022 Note that the off\u2011site travel expense is already committed and to focus on contractors. | Receipt\u00a0r\u20118 (conversation@1, *msg\u201118* + *msg\u201113*) |\n| **Bobby** | \u2022 Take charge of travel scenario analysis.<br>\u2022 Look into downgrading the two tooling renewals. | Receipt\u00a0r\u20118 (conversation@1, *msg\u201120* + *msg\u201117*) |\n| **Carol Corte** | \u2022 Handle the tooling renewals in Q4. | Receipt\u00a0r\u20118 (conversation@1, *msg\u201119*) |\n| **You (ct\u2011self)** | \u2022 Pull the contractor breakdown tomorrow.<br>\u2022 Reconcile the Q4 budget against last quarter. | Receipt\u00a0r\u20118 (conversation@1, *msg\u201115* + *msg\u201121*) |\n\n**Explanation**\n\n1. **Thread participants** were identified via sender IDs in the read conversation \u2013\u202fAlice (`ct-alice`), Bobby (`ct-bob`), Carol (`ct-carol`) and yourself (`ct-self`).\n\n2. **Commitments** were extracted from message bodies:\n   * Alice explicitly tells the team to post proposals by Thursday and notes the off\u2011site commitment.\n   * Bobby says he will take the travel scenarios and can downgrade the renewals.\n   * Carol says she will take the tooling renewals.\n   * You commit to pulling the contractor breakdown and reconciling with last quarter.\n\nThese are the commitments outlined in the thread at the time of the last read.", "answer_hash": "741bc3910809dbade46a187c624f8d50877b355a7d3408f8ce1c2422c60f8262", "kind": "task_end", "receipt_id": "r-10", "seq": 10, "task_id": "t2-group-thread-resolution", "truncated": false, "ts": 1011.0}
